"""
Three-Stage Dedup Pipeline — find fast, verify exactly, explain honestly.

WHAT IT DOES: You have thousands of documents and suspect near-duplicates (reposts,
edited copies, boilerplate). Comparing all pairs is quadratic death. This pipeline:
shingle → MinHash → candidates → exact verify → explain. Cheap signatures prune >80%
of comparisons, real Jaccard verifies survivors, and a word-diff explains why each
pair matched. Each stage covers the previous one's weakness: MinHash is fast but
approximate, edit distance is exact but O(n*m), a diff is readable but only worth
computing for confirmed near-duplicates.

WHEN TO USE: Deduplicating document collections where all-pairs exact comparison is
too expensive and silent deletion is unacceptable (the diff is the audit). Works on
any language (unicode-clean — proven with Ukrainian).

GUARANTEES: All planted near-dup pairs survive verification. No false pairs pass exact
verification. The candidate stage prunes >80% of all-pairs comparisons. The diff
explains what actually differs between matched pairs.

NOT: A production dedup system. No scaling beyond memory, no persistent storage, no
incremental updates. The shingle size k ≤ 0 returns a degenerate signature instead of
erroring (AURA-E009).
"""
